## Closed 3

**#895 — `--output-format json` reports a degraded session. Shipped, taking the reporter's option-2 decision the way they argued it: emit the `external_servers` object always**, because the defect *is* that a consumer can't distinguish degraded from healthy, and a key appearing only on failure forces two shapes — the same defect one layer down. Their drain warning was the sharpest thing in the issue and was exactly right: consuming take_external_failure_note() would have silently deleted the model's note, trading one audience for another. Separate never-drained store, one write site, pinned by a test that reads the JSON then asserts the drain still fires.

